      "notes": "Four problems as listed in the catalogue. Printed sections (A., B., C.) that carry their own points and an introductory text are kept as parts alongside their sub-tasks (A1., A2., …), so the part points of problems 1–3 sum to twice the section totals; the printed section totals are 25 per problem (100 in total), but no problem or paper total is printed, so problem points and totalPoints are null. Problem 1: the statement says 'from А to Г' with Cyrillic letters in the source text layer (kept); the solution uses mg for the weight W and a spring constant K that the statement does not give; the solution prints 71,25 J with a decimal comma (kept). Problem 2: 'the plank’ speed' is printed so (kept). Problem 3: in the A3 solution the final result is printed as v_B(t) = √(2g(H − y_A(t))) — a misprint for v_A, kept verbatim; in B5 the time is printed as '0.71 m' (wrong unit, kept verbatim); the solution restates the introduction of part A with different wording (kept). Problem 4: the solution document is the BPU 2023 problem proposal by Miroslav V. Abrashev and labels the parts a)–h) where the problem sheet uses A.–H.; the statement's table has five empty columns and the solution's table two, reproduced as empty Markdown columns. The semi-sphere figure, the plank figure and the circuit diagram are repeated in the solutions document and are also cut there as solution figures. The BPO logo in the page masthead is decoration and is not cropped. No printed words were corrected. Repaired 2026-10-04 from the independent verification (docs/verification/2026-10-0*-round*) of the agent:opus-5-5 (from-final, published) transcription: restored the printed introductory paragraph of the problem 4 solution (solutions page 10) that had been omitted.",
